{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThree defensive `except`/`isinstance` arms that decide whether an LLM-tier failure ABORTS or\nDEGRADES have **no test that reaches them**. Found by the Step-7 parity sweep while fixing bug\n`wolflike-chevroned-haddock` (`43d4-b8f5-4bb2-417b`). Demonstrated by mutation: reverting each\narm to its pre-fix form (dropping `LLMInputRejectedError` from the tuple) leaves the **entire**\nunit suite green.\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py` mid-run plan-review arm (the\n  `except (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)` around `_ex.run_workflow` in\n  `produce_plan_review_verdict`, ~:189) and the same-shape mid-run code-review arm in\n  `_run_code_review_gate` (~:522).\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/container_stage.py` warm-call abort in `_run_container` (~:209):\n  `isinstance(exc, (LLMUnavailableError, LLMInputRejectedError)) -> raise exc`.\n  `container_stage` has **zero** referencing tests, so the whole module's abort-vs-degrade\n  decision is unpinned.\n\n## Context — reachability analysis (resolves the \"dead code?\" question in the original report)\n\nThe original report noted a probe with a mid-run-raising runner could not reach the\ngate_dispatch arms. Root cause of THAT probe's failure: it raised in the **agent-step** path,\nwhich `interpreter._run_leaf` absorbs into a failed `StepResult` (`except Exception` at the\ndispatch site) — the failure lands in the finders-failed tail, never escaping `run_workflow`.\nThe **batch-step** path is different and IS the raw seam:\n\n- `interpreter._run_batch` calls `runner.run(req, rc.runner)` with **no try** — anything the\n  batch runner raises propagates RAW out of `run_workflow`.\n- Plan-review's `ProductionBatchRunner` -> `run_pass1`: the chunk pool **re-raises**\n  `LLMUnavailableError` (systemic; `pass1.py` warm-chunk comment + the pool's\n  `except LLMUnavailableError: raise`), and the container stage's warm-call abort raises\n  **both** `LLMUnavailableError` and `LLMInputRejectedError` up through `run_pass1`. So the\n  mid-run plan-review arm is **reachable in production** — NOT dead code — and the container\n  abort arm is precisely one of its upstream producers.\n- Code-review's `CodeReviewBatchRunner._run_criterion` translates `LLMUnavailableError` into\n  the kernel's `SystemicDiscoveryError`, which `discovery.execute_stage` **absorbs**\n  (`systemic_abort=True`, no re-raise), and agent steps are absorbed by `_run_leaf` — so no\n  in-tree production raiser for the code-review arm was found. The arm is a **defensive\n  contract at the `run_workflow` seam**. Per the coverage-only mandate this plan does NOT\n  remove it: it pins the contract at the seam and records the reachability finding as a ticket\n  comment (removal, if ever wanted, is a separate design decision).\n\n## Approach — coverage only, zero production-code change\n\nTwo new test files, using established harness patterns only:\n\n1. `tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py`\n   - Plan-review mid-run arm: monkeypatch `rebar.llm.workflow.executor.run_workflow` to raise\n     (a) `LLMUnavailableError`, (b) `LLMInputRejectedError` (the established seam —\n     `test_gate_engine_cutover.py` already monkeypatches `_ex.run_workflow` +\n     `gate_dispatch._gate_doc`); drive `gate_dispatch.produce_plan_review_verdict` with a\n     `FakeRunner` (preflight passes); assert the degraded `INDETERMINATE` verdict\n     (`llm_ran is False`, never PASS) AND the `emit_gate_error` sidecar call (monkeypatched\n     recorder, kwargs-tolerant since the mid-run arm threads `diagnostic=`).\n   - Code-review mid-run arm: same fault injection through\n     `gate_dispatch.produce_code_review_verdict` (`enabled=True` via monkeypatched\n     `code_review_enabled`, `target_ticket` set so the sidecar arm fires, and the WS4\n     `_local_gate_source` autouse fixture copied verbatim — REBAR_GATE_SOURCE=local +\n     delenv REBAR_GATE_REF — to avoid the CI shallow-checkout hang); assert `INDETERMINATE`\n     + sidecar for both exception types.\n   - Seam-fidelity test (ties the monkeypatched seam to reality): a REAL\n     `executor.run_workflow` over a minimal valid batch-step doc (the\n     `tests/unit/workflow/test_batch_step.py` `_wf` shape) with an injected batch runner that\n     raises — assert `pytest.raises(LLMUnavailableError)` and\n     `pytest.raises(LLMInputRejectedError)` propagate RAW (pinning `_run_batch`'s no-try\n     contract that feeds both mid-run arms).\n\n2. `tests/unit/test_container_warm_abort.py` (sibling of `test_container_roster.py`)\n   - Drive the REAL `container_stage._run_container` with `passes.pass1_container`\n     monkeypatched at the model-call boundary (the seam `_timed_pairing` calls). Fixture: a\n     `PlanContext` with `largest_window_tokens=50_000` (budget = 50_000*0.9 - 32_000 =\n     13_000 tokens), plan text ~20_000 chars (~5_000 tokens >= CACHE_MIN_PREFIX_TOKENS 4_096)\n     and two children ~28_000 chars each (~7_000 tokens) so `pack_container_bins` yields two\n     single-child bins -> the warm gate (`parent_tokens >= floor and len(pairings) >= 2`) is\n     MET and the warm call is the first `pass1_container` invocation.\n   - Warm call raises `LLMUnavailableError` -> `pytest.raises`, and exactly ONE\n     `pass1_container` call happened (abort, no fan-out of the remaining pairing).\n   - Warm call raises `LLMInputRejectedError` -> same abort assertions (the 43d4 arm).\n   - Negative control: warm call raises `ValueError` (non-systemic) -> NO raise; degrades to\n     direct fan-out of ALL pairings (3 total calls: 1 failed warm + 2 pool),\n     `coverage[\"container\"][\"warmed\"] is False`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- IN: the two new test files above; a ticket comment recording the reachability analysis and\n  the mutation-check transcript.\n- OUT (non-goals): any change to `gate_dispatch.py`, `container_stage.py`, `pass1.py`,\n  `interpreter.py` or any production module; removing the code-review arm; new lint/CI\n  machinery. If a test exposes a genuine behavioral divergence, a new bug ticket is filed and\n  linked `discovered_from` this one instead of changing gate behavior here.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN mutation protocol)\n\nRED — each new test must be shown to FIRE against the gap it covers, then the mutation is\nreverted:\n- Mutant A: revert BOTH gate_dispatch arms to the pre-43d4 form\n  (`except LLMUnavailableError` only) -> the two input-rejected mid-run tests FAIL (the\n  exception escapes, no degraded verdict).\n- Mutant B: narrow the container isinstance to `LLMUnavailableError` only -> the\n  input-rejected abort test FAILS (degrades to fan-out instead of raising).\n- Mutant C: remove the container abort arm entirely (treat systemic as non-systemic) -> both\n  abort tests FAIL.\nOutputs recorded verbatim in a ticket comment; working tree restored (verified via\n`git diff --stat` clean on `src/`).\n\nGREEN — on unmutated code: the two new files pass, plus the neighboring suites\n(`tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py`, `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws4.py`,\n`tests/unit/workflow/test_batch_step.py`, `tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_warmup.py`).\nGates: `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n(new=0 increased=0). No production file changes -> module-size cap unaffected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Tests reach `gate_dispatch`'s mid-run plan-review arm for BOTH `LLMUnavailableError`\n      and `LLMInputRejectedError` and assert the degraded INDETERMINATE verdict plus the\n      emitted `gate_error_v1` sidecar (`pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_gate_midrun_fail_closed.py -q`).\n- [ ] The same for the mid-run code-review arm; the arm's reachability status (defensive —\n      batch runner translates systemic errors into absorbed kernel signals; no in-tree raw\n      raiser found) is recorded as a ticket comment with the evidence, resolving the\n      original report's remove-or-test question in favor of test-as-seam-contract.\n- [ ] A seam-fidelity test proves a batch runner's `LLMUnavailableError`/`LLMInputRejectedError`\n      propagate RAW out of a real `run_workflow` (pinning `interpreter._run_batch`'s no-try\n      contract that makes the mid-run arms reachable).\n- [ ] Tests drive `container_stage._run_container`'s REAL warm-call path: both systemic types\n      abort the fan-out (raise, exactly one model call); a non-systemic warm failure degrades\n      to direct fan-out (negative control).\n- [ ] Each new test is shown to FAIL under its arm's mutation (Mutants A/B/C above), with the\n      transcript recorded in a ticket comment, and the mutations reverted.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the complexity ratchet pass; no `src/rebar` file is\n      modified by this change."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787381606542514001,"uuid":"08b308ff-c515-4c6e-bcca-945291c35ba4"}